- # `↯/s.98.1` — `Watch.Error`
+ # `↯/s.98.1` — `Watch.Error`

- Raised when Surveillance cannot register a path with the operating
- system's filesystem watcher.
+ Se lanza cuando Surveillance no puede registrar una ruta en el vigilante del sistema de ficheros
+ del sistema operativo.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Surveillance wraps the JDK's `WatchService` API. Several distinct
- conditions can cause registration to fail; the constructor takes
- a `reason: Reason`. The rendered message is `the path could not
- be watched because $reason`.
+ Surveillance envuelve la API `WatchService` del JDK. Varias condiciones distintas pueden hacer que
+ el registro falle; el constructor recibe un `reason: Reason`. El mensaje representado es
+ `the path could not be watched because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.98.1.1` — `LimitExceeded`
+ ### `↯/s.98.1.1` — `LimitExceeded`

- The operating system's per-process or per-user limit on the
- number of inotify (or equivalent) watches has been exceeded.
+ Se ha superado el límite del sistema operativo, por proceso o por usuario, sobre el número de
+ vigilancias de inotify (o equivalentes).

- **Example.** `[↯/s.98.1.1] the path could not be watched because the operating system's limit on watched paths has been exceeded`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.98.1.1] the path could not be watched because the operating system's limit on watched paths has been exceeded`

- **Resolution.** Reduce the number of watched paths, or raise the
- OS limit (e.g. `fs.inotify.max_user_watches` on Linux).
+ **Solución.** Reduce el número de rutas vigiladas, o aumenta el límite del sistema operativo (por
+ ejemplo, `fs.inotify.max_user_watches` en Linux).

- ### `↯/s.98.1.2` — `Nonexistent`
+ ### `↯/s.98.1.2` — `Nonexistent`

- The path passed to `watch` does not exist.
+ La ruta que se pasó a `watch` no existe.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.98.1.2] the path could not be watched because the path does not exist`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.98.1.2] the path could not be watched because the path does not exist`

- **Resolution.** Confirm the path before watching, or create it
- first.
+ **Solución.** Confirma la ruta antes de vigilarla, o créala primero.

- ### `↯/s.98.1.3` — `NotDirectory`
+ ### `↯/s.98.1.3` — `NotDirectory`

- The JDK `WatchService` only registers directories; the supplied
- path was a regular file or other entry.
+ El `WatchService` del JDK solo registra directorios; la ruta proporcionada era un fichero regular
+ u otra entrada.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.98.1.3] the path could not be watched because the path is not a directory`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.98.1.3] the path could not be watched because the path is not a directory`

- **Resolution.** Watch the parent directory and filter events on
- the file name (Surveillance's `watch` extension does this when
- given a file path).
+ **Solución.** Vigila el directorio padre y filtra los eventos por el nombre del fichero (la
+ extensión `watch` de Surveillance lo hace cuando recibe la ruta de un fichero).

- ### `↯/s.98.1.4` — `PermissionDenied`
+ ### `↯/s.98.1.4` — `PermissionDenied`

- The current user does not have permission to read the path.
+ El usuario actual no tiene permiso para leer la ruta.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.98.1.4] the path could not be watched because the user does not have permission to watch the path`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.98.1.4] the path could not be watched because the user does not have permission to watch the path`

- **Resolution.** Adjust filesystem permissions, or run with a user
- that can read the directory.
+ **Solución.** Ajusta los permisos del sistema de ficheros, o ejecuta con un usuario que pueda leer
+ el directorio.

